    "summary": "Model built and all L1/L2/L3 checks pass.\n\nRoot cause of the failure: decision lane.qk was accepted as 10.5 kN/m, the JTG D60-2015 Class I value, but this bridge is Highway Class II. Clause JTGD60-4.3.1-qk requires qk = 10.5 × 0.75 = 7.875 kN/m for Class II, so re-executing the code formula on the model's parameters did not reproduce the stored value and L2-1 failed. Revised lane.qk to 7.875 kN/m (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-qk, INPUT:deck.load_class); the associated lane.Pk.1 = 232.5 kN already carried the correct 0.75 factor.\n\nModel summary:\n- Single simply-supported span, 25 m bearing-centre-to-centre; spine_beam_2d idealization.\n- 5 precast prestressed C40 small-box girders (main-girder self-weight only), A = 5.303 m², I = 1.258 m⁴, Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 137.87 kN/m.\n- Plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×350 mm, 4×8 mm rubber layers) at both abutments, 10 per line, modelled as zero-length springs: S = 10.10, Kv = 1.416e7 kN/m, Kh = 3.28e4 kN/m, rotation free.\n- Class II lane load: qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 232.5 kN, ξ = 0.67 (4 lanes, one-way), μ = 0.241 (from f1).\n\nKey results:\n- Vertical frequencies: 4.272, 16.900, 37.300 Hz.\n- Self-weight support reactions: 1723.3 kN each; midspan self-weight moment 10770.9 kN·m.\n- Max lane-load positive moment 6878.4 kN·m."
